;; The appliance, plus a camera.
;;
;; Everything raspberrypi3-64-bringup serves, and a USB webcam or a CSI
;; camera on top: MJPEG in a browser, MP4 segments, H.264 over RTP. One
;; board that answers four industrial protocols and shows you what the
;; machine looks like, which is closer to a real edge device than either
;; half alone.
;;
;; A Pi 3 is not a Pi 5: four A53 cores at 1.2GHz, and the same missing
;; hardware encoder in the sense that matters here, since Buildroot's
;; GStreamer will not use the Pi's H.264 block. MJPEG straight from a USB
;; camera costs almost nothing because nothing is encoded; x264 at 720p30
;; will not keep up. silt-media's mjpeg mode is the one to use here.
;;
;; The rootfs is larger than the board profile's default: GStreamer,
;; libcamera-apps and ffmpeg are not small, and /var/www/rec fills with
;; recordings.

(image raspberrypi3-64-media
  (compose
    image:raspberrypi3-64-bringup
    feature:media-kit)

  (override
    (value buildroot:BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE "2G"))

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
